  "body": "Hello,\r\n\r\nI installed Matrix on my server today with the domain `matrix.domain.org`. I just realized, that my server isn't federating, so I tried the Matrix Federation tester with `matrix.domain.org`.\r\n\r\nWell, it seems like port `8448` isn't reachable. So I tried adding a VirtualHost in the Apache config of Matrix. I then started to search for solutions and found following thread: https://github.com/matrix-org/matrix-federation-tester/issues/93. I tried understanding it, but it seems like I'm missing something. As far as I understood, I somehow need to make a reverse proxy on my domain `domain.org` with port `8448`, redirects to `8008`?\r\n\r\nI tried it and it doesn't work. I also should mention that my homepage (`domain.org`) is behind Cloudflare, but my Matrix server is not. \r\n\r\nHere are my two Apache2 configs. One for matrix, one for my \"main page\".\r\n\r\n - `domain.org`: https://ghostbin.me/648766326d471\r\n - `matrix.domain.org`: https://ghostbin.me/648765ca08840\r\n - Matrix config: https://ghostbin.me/64876afd2fd04\r\n\r\nDoes anyone have tips how I can fix that? I installed Matrix via docker.",
